## Third-party material, and one correction

### The corpus is fetched, not vendored

`references/battleships/` is the `ariana-dot-dev/battleships` provider corpus.
**It carries no licence.** The GitHub API reports `license: null` for that
repository and its tree contains no `LICENSE` file:

    gh api repos/ariana-dot-dev/battleships --jq .license    # null
    gh api repos/ariana-dot-dev/battleships/license          # 404 Not Found

Earlier revisions of this repository committed all 1183 of its files (13 MB)
inside a 0BSD project. That granted redistribution rights over somebody else's
work that nobody had granted, so the corpus is no longer committed. It is a
build input, restored by:

    bash experiments/10-fetch-corpus.sh

at the pinned commit `f6a71ab09fefa68e355ef47c52315e099f99c921`.

**What this costs.** The corpus is no longer readable without running that
script, so every figure in `docs/CATALOGUE.md` and `data/*.json` is
checkable rather than diffable. If upstream is rewritten and the pinned commit
becomes unreachable, this repository's inputs are gone and the method is dead;
`10-fetch-corpus.sh` exits 1 in that case and says so.

### Provider pages are not committed

No provider pricing page is stored here. `experiments/50-firstparty-audit.py`
re-fetches them live and records the HTTP status, byte count and the figures it
matched in `data/firstparty-audit.json`. Short price strings quoted in
`docs/FINDINGS.md` are quoted for verification, not relicensed.

## What is definitely wrong here

This is a research pass, not a product. It is a shape ranking, not a fit
ranking; it inherits every price error in one corpus at one commit; and 440
figures in the first-party sample could not be confirmed. Read section 0 of
`docs/FINDINGS.md` before any table.
